# The client is one page at `/`, so every path that is not a real file has to serve it.
#
# `/n/<petname>/` — and `/n/<service>.<petname>/` for one of that machine's dashboards — is the
# route that opens a machine's page in an iframe. The service worker answers it before the network
# is ever consulted — but on the very first load, before the worker is installed, that URL goes to
# the host, and a 404 there puts the browser into a dead frame on exactly the request that matters.
# Serving the page is correct: the worker takes over from there.
#
# `200` is a rewrite, not a redirect: the URL the client sees stays `/n/<target>/`, which is what
# the worker keys on to know which node and which of its services it is answering for.
/*    /index.html    200
